<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Raetia</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Rhaetia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Raetia was a Roman province in the central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alps">Alps</a> and the Alpine foreland, covering parts of modern eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a>, southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> and northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>. Conquered by Drusus and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiberius">Tiberius</a> in 15 BCE, it had its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/augusta-vindelicorum">Augusta Vindelicorum</a> (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/augsburg">Augsburg</a>) and guarded the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> frontier against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germanic-peoples">Germanic peoples</a> such as the Alemanni and Juthungi.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/raetia.jpg" alt="Raetia" width="320" height="267" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Milenioscuro · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Roman_Empire_-_Raetia_(125_AD).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
